From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:51:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: hash a shader stage that names no shader

vk_pipeline_hash_shader_stage_blake3() hashes a stage by its module, by a
VkShaderModuleCreateInfo chained to it, or by a module identifier, and
asserted that the identifier was there when the first two were not.  A
release build compiles the assert out, so a stage with a null module and
nothing chained read the identifier through a null pointer, and an
identifier that names a size but no bytes read through another.  The entry
point name was measured with strlen() whether or not it was there.  The
Venus renderer runs in the application's own process on Apple hosts, and its
driver is handed whatever a guest sends, so each ended the process.

Hash nothing of the shader for a stage that names none, and nothing of an
absent name or identifier.  Building such a stage already fails in
vk_pipeline_shader_stage_to_nir() with "No shader module provided"; give an
absent entry point name the same refusal there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
index 0a3eac7238e78bf15c711b979c98d6f5ba2774ce..f159e5d1875823eb1cf7989d6956cd6a8381c4ed 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -192,6 +192,11 @@ vk_pipeline_shader_stage_to_nir(struct vk_device *device,
       return VK_SUCCESS;
    }
 
+   if (unlikely(info->pName == NULL)) {
+      return vk_errorf(device, VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN,
+                       "No shader entry point name provided");
+   }
+
    const uint32_t *spirv_data;
    uint32_t spirv_size;
    if (module != NULL) {
@@ -284,18 +289,25 @@ vk_pipeline_hash_shader_stage_blake3(VkPipelineCreateFlags2KHR pipeline_flags,
       blake3_hash module_hash;
       vk_shader_module_hash(minfo, module_hash);
       _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, module_hash, sizeof(module_hash));
-   } else {
+   } else if (iinfo != NULL) {
       /* It is legal to pass in arbitrary identifiers as long as they don't exceed
        * the limit. Shaders with bogus identifiers are more or less guaranteed to fail. */
-      assert(iinfo);
       assert(iinfo->identifierSize <= VK_MAX_SHADER_MODULE_IDENTIFIER_SIZE_EXT);
-      _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, iinfo->pIdentifier, iinfo->identifierSize);
+      if (iinfo->pIdentifier != NULL)
+         _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, iinfo->pIdentifier, iinfo->identifierSize);
    }
+   /* A stage with no module, no chained module and no identifier names no
+    * shader at all, which the specification does not allow.  Its hash holds
+    * nothing of a shader, and building it fails in
+    * vk_pipeline_shader_stage_to_nir.
+    */
 
    if (rstate)
       _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, rstate, sizeof(*rstate));
 
-   _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, info->pName, strlen(info->pName));
+   /* An absent entry point name fails in vk_pipeline_shader_stage_to_nir. */
+   if (info->pName != NULL)
+      _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, info->pName, strlen(info->pName));
 
    if (info->pSpecializationInfo) {
       _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, info->pSpecializationInfo->pMapEntries,
